# Normalise text to LF in every working tree, whatever the OS.
#
# Everything here that executes does so inside Linux containers. A Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise write CRLF, and then:
#
#   - the shell scripts die in the container on the first line ending in \r
#     (`set: illegal option -`), including the init hook the database runs on
#     first boot, so the stack never comes up;
#   - the migrations hash differently. The runner stores a sha256 of each file,
#     so a database migrated from a CRLF checkout and later handled from an LF
#     one reports every migration as edited-since-applied and refuses to run.
#
# `text=auto` leaves genuinely binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
